The Largest Arrival in the BUSINESS.

MARX LEVIHSON,
Nearly opposite the Kosluk Hotel.

MR. LEVIHSON begs leave to inform his friends in

San Francisco, and vicinity, that he has returned from
San Francisco, with extensive and fashionable stock of
summer clothing, Boots, Shoes, HATS, Caps, etc., as can
be found in any Store in the mines. Ne stock consists
mainly of
Pine Cloth Frock Coats;
Fine Serge Sack Coats;
Linen and Muslins do;
Drabs, Lasting, and Drab do;
Linen and Muslin Waist;
Black and Blue colored Do.
Muslins, Linen and Muslin do;
Fine, Linen and Muslins Vests;
Davis Coats, white and Coated Shirts;
Cotton, Linen and Cotton Finishing Goods;
Fine Cropped Boots, Galoshes and Pumps
Goodly Heavy Calf Lining Boots;
Silk Handkerchiefs and Cravats;

Latest Styles of Hats and Thousand different articles
too numerous to mention, but all suitable. Call
and see me. MARX LEVIHSON.
Raleighville, May 18th, 1858.

THE subscriber would respectfully
announce to the citizens of Wilmington and
the public generally, that he has just selected in person, the manufactures will receive
during this month, the largest assorted stock of Cabinet
Furniture that he has offered this place. As he
has had long experience in this business and having pur-
chased his entire stock for cash, at manufacturers' cash
prices, he offers inducements to purchasers.
The following among the articles to be found in his
store, viz.

Parlor Sets, complete in Mahogany and Walnut;
Brocatene and hair-cloth covering;
Sofas and Tete Tetes, great variety from $3 to $50;
Mahogany and Walnut, Upholstered Rocking and Easy
Chairs;
Ottomans, Etageres and Corner Stands;
Centre, Sofa and Card Tables;
Pier, Mantle and Oval Mirrors;
Cane Seat Chairs from 15 cents to $23 each;
Cane seat Rocking and Nurse Chairs;
Sideboards and Secretaries;
beautiful lot of Chamber Furniture, sets complete;
bureaus, great variety, from $1 to $50;
Wardrobes, Washstands, Marble top, &c.;
Bedsteads, Bedsteads, Bedsteads;
Towel and light Stands;
Extension and other dining Tables;
Work Tables, Toilet Tables, Teapoys, &c.;
Also lot of superior Piano Fortes, Music Stands, Stools
&c.

Intending to sell goods on his terms are cash, or good negotiable paper 50 days, with interest added.

JOHN D. LOVE,

No. 10 Front street, Wilmington N. C.
August 19, 1857
